WEBVTT

00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:00.973
[boy] This is Berk.

00:01:01.148 --> 00:01:02.845
It's twelve days north
of hopeless

00:01:03.019 --> 00:01:05.500
and a few degrees south
of freezing to death.

00:01:05.674 --> 00:01:08.894
It's located solidly
on the meridian of misery.

00:01:10.113 --> 00:01:13.638
My village.
In a word, sturdy.

00:01:13.812 --> 00:01:18.643
It's been here for seven
generations, but every
single building is new.

00:01:18.817 --> 00:01:22.821
We have fishing, hunting
and a charming view
of the sunsets.

00:01:22.995 --> 00:01:26.782
The only problems
are the pests.

00:01:26.956 --> 00:01:30.481
You see, most places
have mice or mosquitoes.

00:01:30.655 --> 00:01:32.962
We have...

00:01:35.704 --> 00:01:38.054
...dragons.

00:01:38.228 --> 00:01:41.101
[boy] Most people
would leave. Not us.

00:01:41.275 --> 00:01:44.756
We're Vikings. We have
stubbornness issues.

00:01:46.758 --> 00:01:48.804
My name is Hiccup.

00:01:48.978 --> 00:01:51.720
Great name, I know.
But it's not the worst.

00:01:51.894 --> 00:01:55.506
Parents believe a hideous
name will frighten off
gnomes and trolls.

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:57.639
Like our charming Viking
demeanor wouldn't do that.

00:01:57.813 --> 00:01:59.945
[roars] Morning!

00:02:02.078 --> 00:02:04.080
- What are you doing here?!
- Get inside!

00:02:04.254 --> 00:02:06.604
- What are you doing out?!
- Get back inside!

00:02:09.172 --> 00:02:11.740
Hiccup!
What is he doing...?

00:02:11.914 --> 00:02:13.959
What are you doing out?!
Get inside!

00:02:14.134 --> 00:02:17.833
[Hiccup] That's Stoick
the Vast, chief of the tribe.

00:02:18.007 --> 00:02:22.838
They say when he was a baby,
he popped a dragon's head
clean off its shoulders.

00:02:23.012 --> 00:02:24.796
Do I believe it?
Yes, I do.

00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:26.276
What have we got?

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:28.017
Gronckles. Nadders.
Zipplebacks.

00:02:28.191 --> 00:02:30.498
Oh, and Hoark saw
a Monstrous Nightmare.

00:02:31.847 --> 00:02:33.588
- Any Night Furies?
- [man] None so far.

00:02:33.762 --> 00:02:34.719
Good.

00:02:34.893 --> 00:02:36.721
[man 2] Hoist the torches!

00:02:36.895 --> 00:02:37.983
[grunts]

00:02:42.684 --> 00:02:44.686
Oh! Nice of you
to join the party!

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:46.514
I thought you'd been
carried off!

00:02:46.688 --> 00:02:50.953
Who, me? Come on,
I'm way too muscular
for their taste.

00:02:51.127 --> 00:02:54.043
They wouldn't know
what to do with all this.

00:02:54.217 --> 00:02:57.046
They need toothpicks,
don't they?

00:02:57.220 --> 00:02:58.700
[Hiccup] The meathead
with attitude

00:02:58.874 --> 00:03:00.745
and interchangeable
hands is Gobber.

00:03:00.919 --> 00:03:03.008
I've been his apprentice
since I was little.

00:03:03.183 --> 00:03:05.750
Well, littler.

00:03:05.924 --> 00:03:09.189
Move to the lower defenses.
We'll counterattack
with the catapults.

00:03:11.974 --> 00:03:15.107
See? Old village, lots
and lots of new houses.

00:03:15.282 --> 00:03:16.718
Fire!

00:03:16.892 --> 00:03:18.372
[girl] Let's go!

00:03:18.546 --> 00:03:20.896
[Hiccup]
That's Fishlegs, Snotlout,

00:03:21.070 --> 00:03:22.593
the twins:
Ruffnut and Tuffnut...

00:03:22.767 --> 00:03:24.856
...and...

00:03:26.031 --> 00:03:28.033
...Astrid.

00:03:37.782 --> 00:03:39.915
Oh, their job
is so much cooler.

00:03:40.089 --> 00:03:43.092
- Eh!
- Come on. Let me out, please.

00:03:43.266 --> 00:03:44.963
I need to make
my mark.

00:03:45.137 --> 00:03:47.662
You've made plenty of marks,
all in the wrong places.

00:03:47.836 --> 00:03:49.751
Please, two minutes.
I'll kill a dragon.

00:03:49.925 --> 00:03:53.189
My life will get
infinitely better.
I might even get a date.

00:03:53.363 --> 00:03:55.757
You can't lift a hammer.
You can't swing an axe.

00:03:55.931 --> 00:03:57.149
You can't even throw
one of these!

00:03:59.978 --> 00:04:02.894
OK, fine, but this
will throw it for me.

00:04:03.068 --> 00:04:04.722
- Ohh!
- [groans]

00:04:04.896 --> 00:04:07.508
See? Now this right here
is what I'm talking about!

00:04:07.682 --> 00:04:09.814
- [stammers] Mild
calibration issue...
- Hiccup!

00:04:09.988 --> 00:04:12.991
If you ever want to get out
there to fight dragons...

00:04:13.165 --> 00:04:15.994
...you need to stop
all this.

00:04:16.168 --> 00:04:18.083
But you just pointed
to all of me.

00:04:18.258 --> 00:04:21.086
Yes, that's it!
Stop being all of you.

00:04:21.261 --> 00:04:24.089
- Ohh...
- Oh, yes.

00:04:24.264 --> 00:04:26.875
You, sir, are playing
a dangerous game.

00:04:27.049 --> 00:04:31.140
Keeping this much
raw Vikingness contained?

00:04:31.314 --> 00:04:33.098
There will be
consequences!

00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:36.232
I'll take my chances.
Sword. Sharpen. Now.

00:04:37.973 --> 00:04:40.105
[Hiccup] One day,
I'll get out there.

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:41.977
Because killing
a dragon...

00:04:42.151 --> 00:04:45.110
...is everything
around here.

00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:48.723
A Nadder head is sure
to get me at least noticed.

00:04:48.897 --> 00:04:51.726
Gronckles are tough.
Taking down one of those

00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:53.728
would definitely
get me a girlfriend.

00:04:54.729 --> 00:04:55.817
A Zippleback?

00:04:55.991 --> 00:04:57.819
- [spits]
- [people scream]

00:04:57.993 --> 00:04:59.908
[Hiccup] Exotic. Two heads,
twice the status.

00:05:00.082 --> 00:05:01.518
They found the sheep!

00:05:01.692 --> 00:05:03.694
Concentrate fire
over the lower bank.

00:05:03.868 --> 00:05:06.262
- Fire!
- [grunts]

00:05:06.436 --> 00:05:09.352
And then there's
the Monstrous Nightmare.

00:05:09.526 --> 00:05:12.224
Only the best Vikings
go after those.

00:05:12.399 --> 00:05:15.706
They have this nasty habit
of setting themselves on fire.

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:17.926
[snarling]

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:20.102
Reload!
I'll take care of this.

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:25.977
But the ultimate prize
is the dragon no one's
ever seen.

00:05:26.151 --> 00:05:28.023
- We call it the...
- Night Fury!

00:05:28.197 --> 00:05:30.155
- Get down!
- [screams]

00:05:32.767 --> 00:05:34.899
Jump!

00:05:35.073 --> 00:05:39.034
This thing never steals food,
never shows itself, and...

00:05:40.383 --> 00:05:42.211
...never misses.

00:05:42.385 --> 00:05:44.648
No one has ever killed
a Night Fury.

00:05:44.822 --> 00:05:47.129
That's why I'm going
to be the first.

00:05:47.303 --> 00:05:50.219
Man the fort, Hiccup.
They need me out there.

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:54.397
Stay. Put. There.

00:05:56.051 --> 00:05:58.836
You know what I mean.
[yells]

00:05:59.010 --> 00:06:01.056
- [man] Where are you going?
- Yeah, I know!

00:06:01.230 --> 00:06:03.188
- [woman] Hiccup!
- Be right back!

00:06:04.146 --> 00:06:06.191
[sheep braying]

00:06:08.498 --> 00:06:09.760
[man] Let's get 'em!

00:06:09.934 --> 00:06:12.110
[Stoick] Mind yourselves!

00:06:12.284 --> 00:06:14.243
The devils still have
some juice in them!

00:06:16.376 --> 00:06:17.377
[grunts]

